cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Asclepios in published work, please cite it as below."
title: "Asclepios: an open-source finite element solver"
type: software
authors:
  - alias: NonameAccountMax
repository-code: "https://github.com/NonameAccountMax/Asclepios"
url: "https://github.com/NonameAccountMax/Asclepios"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  Lightweight C++17 finite element solver for nonlinear structural dynamics of
  soft tissues and slender devices: explicit dynamics, static implicit analysis,
  shells, beams, connectors, hyperelastic and elasto-plastic materials, and
  general contact. It reads a subset of the Abaqus keyword input format.
keywords:
  - finite element method
  - explicit dynamics
  - nonlinear mechanics
  - biomechanics
  - medical devices
  - shells
  - contact
